# Club & Grub - World 1, stage 2 co-op: "Canopy Village" for two (designer DB1; docs/expansion/DESIGN.md D.9).
# The co-op file of levels/w1_l2.lvl (kind = coop, coop_of, coop_base_hash; never edit the solo file). Gate 1
# "treehouse": the floor lift is gone - the first tree house stands 8 rows over a root mound at its foot, and only a
# Shoulder Hop (or a Totem launch) gets one hero up; he clubs the coiled vine at the deck's edge down for the
# other. Gate 2 "shaft": the upper branches of the trunk climb are gone; the way to the trunk top leads through the
# trunk room, now a shaft whose ledge is 8 rows over its floor - too high for a Totem Ride jump: one hero lands on his
# partner's head holding Up (the Shoulder Hop) or jumps just after him from his head (the Totem launch), and up there
# crouches on a plate: a stone lifts his partner to the ledge; a hanging vine takes both to the trunk top (the wf10
# redesign of the pulley). The Feast Land A warp in the crow's nest waits in a cage
# that twin drums open (one on the trunk top, one on the big branch). Leapers in two pits of the lower deck, a
# Snatcher bat over the big branch, Shellback turtles and lone stingers (the solo file's pterodactyl is left out: it
# circles its target through the trunk wall, and a head bounce on it lifts a lone hero up the shaft - G22); the x2
# secret is the treetop cache over the village deck, 8 rows up: a charged Batter Up lob (crouch to charge, then the
# high strike) reaches it - Cave Painting 21.

[meta]
format = 2
id = w1_l2_coop
name = "Canopy Village"
kind = coop
coop_of = w1_l2
coop_base_hash = "5b9d4436f427f4f99120306cc79421003a0998734a5d5fe5f8c367350ecaf67f"
book = 1
world = 1
stage = 2
biome = jungle
terrain_a = jungle/terrain
terrain_b = jungle/terrain_grass
background = jungle
music = level_jungle
liquid = water
bonus = bonus_a
bonus_tier = 0
author = DB1
notes = "Co-op 1-2: boost ledge to the tree house (rolled vine back), Shoulder Hop ledge with a plate-driven lift stone in the trunk shaft, drum-caged warp, two leaper pits, Snatcher bat, treetop cache by charged lob (painting 21)."

